<div class="quiz"><div class="quiz__top-bar"><div class="quiz__score-tracker" style="display:none;"></div><button class="quiz__start-over" type="button" style="display:none;">Start Over</button></div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q1d">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">1</span> <div><p><strong>Sartre claims (1) there are no objective moral norms, and (2) bad faith is wrong. Which of the following is the most serious philosophical challenge this creates for his position?</strong></p></div></div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q1" value="q1a" id="q1a">
        <label for="q1a">Without objective norms, Sartre cannot distinguish better and worse political systems</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q1" value="q1b" id="q1b">
        <label for="q1b">The condemnation of bad faith requires appealing to a fixed human nature, which contradicts "existence precedes essence"</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q1" value="q1c" id="q1c">
        <label for="q1c">Sartre's denial of objective norms means he cannot consistently hold any view about anything</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q1" value="q1d" id="q1d">
        <label for="q1d">If values are the products of individual choice and there are no objective norms, it is unclear on what basis bad faith can be condemned as wrong rather than merely inconvenient</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. This is the central tension in Sartre's ethics. If moral norms are products of individual choice, what makes the choice to live in bad faith worse than the choice to live authentically? Sartre's defenders argue that the condemnation of bad faith follows not from an external norm but from the internal structure of consciousness itself — bad faith is incoherent because it relies on and denies the same freedom simultaneously. Whether this response works is a genuine open question.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;"></div>
  </div>
